module rtPCR_N1_Detection
module rtPCR_N2_Detection
module rtPCR_RnaseP_Detection
module ddPCR_N1_Detection
module ddPCR_N2_Detection
module ddPCR_RnaseP_Detection

manifest SalivaSpecimen
manifest NasalSwabSpecimen
manifest TrizolLS_Reagent
manifest Chloroform
manifest Isopropanol
manifest Glycogen
manifest Ethanol_75pct
manifest RNaseFreeWater
manifest TaqPath_MasterMix
manifest N1_ProbePrimerSet
manifest N2_ProbePrimerSet
manifest RnaseP_ProbePrimerSet
manifest PrecisionBlue_RTDye
manifest SARS_CoV2_RNA_Standard
manifest ddPCR_Supermix_OneStep
manifest ReverseTranscriptase_DTT
manifest DropletGeneratorOil
manifest QubitRNA_HS_Reagent

// ============================================================
// Sensitive Detection and Quantification of SARS-CoV-2 in Saliva
// Abasiyanik et al., Scientific Reports (2021) 11:12425
// DOI: 10.1038/s41598-021-91835-7
//
// Protocol: Saliva-based SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid detection
// using TRIzol-based RNA extraction followed by parallel
// RT-PCR and ddPCR readouts. Specimens collected from curbside
// outpatients (N=137) and COVID-19 inpatients (N=29) at the
// University of Chicago Medical Center (IRB 20-0520).
//
// SAMPLE COLLECTION SUMMARY:
//   Saliva: patients spit until sterile tube filled to 2 mL
//   line; 2 mL Zymo DNA/RNA Shield (ZymoR1100-50) added
//   immediately. Nasal swab (NS) collected into 1 mL Amies
//   transport solution (Thermo Scientific).
//
// RNA EXTRACTION (TRIzol-based, TRE method):
//   1 mL saliva + 3 mL TRIzol LS + 0.6 mL chloroform
//   -> centrifuge 15 min at 12,000xg, 4 C
//   -> transfer 0.8 mL aqueous phase + 1 mL isopropanol
//      + 1 uL glycogen; keep at -20 C overnight
//   -> centrifuge 10 min at 12,000xg, 4 C; discard supernatant
//   -> resuspend pellet in 2 mL 75% ethanol
//   -> centrifuge 5 min at 7500g, 4 C; discard supernatant
//   -> incubate pellet 5-10 min at room temperature
//   -> resuspend in 50 uL RNase-free water
//   -> QC: Qubit RNA HS kit; store at -80 C
//   Relative efficiency of TRE vs QVK (QIAmp Viral RNA): 17%.
//   High assay sensitivity compensates for lower yield.
//
// RT-PCR ASSAY (20 uL reaction):
//   5 uL TaqPath One-Step RT-PCR Master Mix (ThermoFisher)
//   2 uL N1, N2, or RnaseP probe/primers (IDT, #10006770)
//   0.1 uL Precision Blue Real-Time PCR Dye (Bio-Rad)
//   6.4 uL RNA extract
//   6.5 uL PCR-grade water
//   Positive control: SARS-CoV-2 RNA Standard (Exact Diagnostics #COV019)
//   CFX384 Touch (Bio-Rad); CDC 2019-nCoV protocol (Revision 3):
//   25 C/2 min -> 50 C/15 min -> 95 C/2 min -> 45x(95 C/3s, 55 C/30s)
//   Call positive: Ct < 40 for N1 OR N2 (CDC recommendation).
//   RnaseP: internal control for extraction quality.
//   Efficiency: >99.25% for both N1 and N2 (Supplementary Fig. 1).
//   LOD: 1 copy/reaction (Ct ~38.2 for N1, ~38.6 for N2).
//
// ddPCR ASSAY (20 uL reaction):
//   5 uL One-step ddPCR Supermix (Bio-Rad)
//   2 uL reverse transcriptase (Bio-Rad)
//   1 uL 300 mM DTT (Bio-Rad)
//   2 uL N1/N2/RnaseP probe/primers (IDT, #10006770)
//   6.4 uL RNA extract
//   -> droplet generation (~20,000 nanoliter-sized droplets)
//   -> C-1000 thermal cycler (Bio-Rad):
//      25 C/2 min -> 50 C/60 min -> 95 C/10 min
//      -> 45x(95 C/30s, 55 C/60s) -> 98 C/10 min -> 4 C hold
//      (ramping speed: 2.5 C/s)
//   -> QX200 droplet reader (Bio-Rad)
//   -> Quantasoft downstream analysis
//   Call positive (NS): CN/uL > 0.1 AND > 2 positive droplets
//      for N1 OR N2 (Bio-Rad manufacturer recommendation).
//   Call positive (saliva): empirical threshold (mean + 2*SD
//      from 45 SARS-CoV-2 negative pre-operative cohort;
//      Supplementary Table 2). Both CN/uL concentration AND
//      positive droplet count must exceed threshold.
//   LOD: 0.06 CN/uL (N1), 0.21 CN/uL (N2); detects virus
//      at 1:1,000,000 dilution in pool of negatives
//      (Supplementary Table 1).
//
// POSITIVE CALLING SUMMARY (Curbside, N=92):
//   RT-PCR saliva: 16/16 CML positives detected (100% sensitivity)
//                  + 7 additional positives missed by CML NS assay
//   ddPCR saliva: 15/16 CML positives detected (93.75% sensitivity)
//                 + 16 additional positives vs CML NS assay
//   (Fig. 2c-f, paper Section "High concordance...")
//
// INPATIENT COHORT (N=29):
//   RT-PCR saliva: 14/14 CML positives detected (100%)
//                  + 9 additional positives vs CML NS assay
//   ddPCR saliva: 11/14 CML positives; 17 total positives
//   (Fig. 5, paper Section "Inpatient specimens")
//
// NOTE ON BioScript ABSTRACTIONS:
//   - TRIzol-based RNA extraction is modelled as a sequence of
//     mix (phase separation, resuspension) and heat (incubation,
//     precipitation) steps. Centrifugation steps (which have no
//     direct BioScript primitive) are abstracted as heat steps
//     at 4 C for their respective durations, consistent with
//     the reference BioScript files' use of heat for non-heating
//     physical operations (e.g., samlali uses heat at 25 C to
//     model electrode actuation).
//   - ddPCR droplet generation and thermocycling are modelled
//     as a heat sequence; the droplet reader readout is modelled
//     as a detect call using the ddPCR detection modules.
//   - RT-PCR thermocycling is modelled as a heat sequence
//     followed by detect calls using the RT-PCR detection modules.
//   - `mix` steps abstracting physical reagent combination
//     (pipetting, aqueous-phase transfer) are labelled with
//     "NOTE: abstracts [operation]" in inline comments.
//   - Parallel N1 and N2 assays (both RT-PCR and ddPCR) are
//     run from the same extracted RNA aliquots. Both channels
//     are encoded as sequential detect calls; the positive-
//     calling OR logic is implemented in the QC gate (if/else).
//   - RnaseP detection is run as an independent internal control
//     channel; its result is not used in the positive/negative
//     QC gate but is encoded for completeness per paper Methods.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS:
//   BioScript (lilott8/BioScript) accepts only `s` (seconds)
//   and `m` (minutes) as duration tokens. All durations from
//   the paper are converted:
//     overnight (-20 C): approximated as 720m (12 h minimum
//     per standard molecular biology practice; paper states
//     "overnight or room temperature for 10 min" -- the cold
//     precipitation path is encoded here as it is the primary
//     method used for high-yield extraction).
//     5-10 min ethanol evaporation: encoded as 10m (upper bound).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: sample receipt, TRIzol RNA
//                             extraction, QC, RT-PCR thermocycle,
//                             ddPCR thermocycle
//   BB2  rtPCR_Pass        -- rtPCR_N1_Signal > 0 OR rtPCR_N2_Signal > 0:
//                             sample RT-PCR positive; dispose
//   BB3  rtPCR_Fail        -- both signals <= 0: RT-PCR negative; drain
//   BB4  rtPCR_Join        -- join: ddPCR QC gate begins
//   BB5  ddPCR_Pass        -- ddPCR_N1_Signal > 0 OR ddPCR_N2_Signal > 0:
//                             sample ddPCR positive; dispose
//   BB6  ddPCR_Fail        -- both signals <= 0: ddPCR negative; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Receipt of saliva specimen.
//   Patient saliva collected at curbside facility by spitting
//   into sterile tube to the 2 mL line; immediately mixed
//   with 2 mL Zymo DNA/RNA Shield (ZymoR1100-50) by the
//   research team. Specimen transported to BSL3 facility
//   for RNA extraction.
//   NOTE: `dispense` abstracts receipt of pre-stabilised
//   1 mL saliva aliquot entering the extraction protocol.
//   The Zymo shield is already incorporated in the specimen
//   manifest at this stage (as added at collection point).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

salivaSpecimen = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Add TRIzol LS Reagent.
//   3 mL TRIzol LS (Thermo Fisher Scientific, #10296010)
//   added to 1 mL saliva (or nasal swab) specimen.
//   TRIzol lyses cells and denatures proteins; guanidinium
//   thiocyanate protects RNA from RNases during extraction.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts manual pipetting addition and
//   brief vortexing to homogenise the sample.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trizolReagent    = dispense 3 units of TrizolLS_Reagent
trizolLysate     = mix salivaSpecimen with trizolReagent for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Add chloroform for phase separation.
//   0.6 mL chloroform added to TRIzol lysate; vortexed
//   briefly to create an emulsion. Chloroform separates
//   the organic (protein/DNA) phase from the aqueous
//   (RNA-containing) upper phase.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts addition and vortexing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chloroformVol    = dispense 1 units of Chloroform
phaseMixture     = mix trizolLysate with chloroformVol for 15s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Centrifugation - phase separation (12,000xg, 4 C, 15 min).
//   The emulsion separates into three phases:
//   (1) colourless upper aqueous phase (RNA)
//   (2) white interphase (DNA/protein)
//   (3) red-pink organic phase (protein/lipid)
//   NOTE: `heat` at 4 C for 15 min abstracts centrifugation
//   (12,000xg, 4 C, 15 min). This is consistent with
//   reference BioScript abstractions (samlali: heat at 25 C
//   models 30 s electrode actuation; moazami: heat at 4 C
//   models cold-shock recovery). Centrifugation has no
//   native BioScript primitive.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat phaseMixture at 4c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Transfer aqueous phase + add isopropanol + glycogen.
//   0.8 mL of the colourless upper aqueous phase is carefully
//   transferred (avoiding the interphase) to a new tube.
//   1 mL isopropanol and 1 uL glycogen are added.
//   Glycogen (1 uL) acts as a co-precipitant to improve RNA
//   pellet visibility and recovery at low concentrations.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the careful pipette transfer and
//   addition of isopropanol and glycogen.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

aqueousPhase     = dispense 1 units of RNaseFreeWater
isopropanolVol   = dispense 1 units of Isopropanol
glycogenVol      = dispense 1 units of Glycogen

// NOTE: abstracts aqueous-phase transfer from centrifuge tube
rnaPrecipMix1    = mix phaseMixture with isopropanolVol for 10s
rnaPrecipMix2    = mix rnaPrecipMix1 with glycogenVol for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Overnight precipitation at -20 C.
//   Mixture kept at -20 C overnight to precipitate RNA.
//   Paper states "overnight or room temperature for 10 min";
//   the -20 C overnight path is encoded here as it gives
//   higher RNA yield and is used for research-grade extraction.
//   NOTE: `heat` at -20 C (encoded as 4 C minimum, closest
//   BioScript-supported cold temperature) for 720 min (12 h)
//   abstracts the -20 C overnight precipitation step.
//   The BioScript compiler accepts negative temperature values;
//   if compiler rejects -20c, substitute 4c as functional
//   approximation for the cold precipitation abstraction.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaPrecipMix2 at 4c for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Centrifugation - RNA pellet collection (12,000xg, 4 C, 10 min).
//   Centrifuge to collect RNA pellet. Supernatant discarded.
//   NOTE: `heat` at 4 C for 10 min abstracts centrifugation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaPrecipMix2 at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Wash pellet with 75% ethanol (2 mL).
//   Pellet resuspended in 2 mL 75% ethanol; vortexed to wash
//   away residual isopropanol and salts that would inhibit
//   downstream PCR reactions (salivary fluids are known PCR
//   inhibitors; see paper reference 14).
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts pellet resuspension and vortexing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ethanolWash      = dispense 2 units of Ethanol_75pct
rnaEthanolWash   = mix rnaPrecipMix2 with ethanolWash for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Centrifugation - ethanol wash (7,500g, 4 C, 5 min).
//   Centrifuge to re-pellet RNA; discard ethanol supernatant.
//   NOTE: `heat` at 4 C for 5 min abstracts centrifugation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaEthanolWash at 4c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Ethanol evaporation (room temperature, 5-10 min).
//   Pellet incubated at room temperature for 5-10 min to
//   evaporate residual ethanol. Over-drying reduces yield;
//   under-drying causes ethanol carry-over inhibition.
//   Encoded as 10 min (upper bound per paper Methods).
//   NOTE: `heat` at 25 C for 10 min abstracts air-drying.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaEthanolWash at 25c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Resuspend RNA pellet in 50 uL RNase-free water.
//   Final RNA extract in 50 uL; stored at -80 C until use.
//   Quantity and quality assessed using Qubit RNA HS Kit
//   before proceeding to PCR assays.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts resuspension. QubitRNA_HS_Reagent
//   dispense represents the QC measurement step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rnaseFreWater2   = dispense 1 units of RNaseFreeWater
rnaExtract       = mix rnaEthanolWash with rnaseFreWater2 for 2m

qubitReagent     = dispense 1 units of QubitRNA_HS_Reagent
rnaQcMix         = mix rnaExtract with qubitReagent for 2m
rnaQcSignal      = detect ddPCR_RnaseP_Detection on rnaQcMix for 30s
dispose rnaQcMix

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Prepare RT-PCR reactions (20 uL total, 3 channels).
//   Three parallel reactions targeting N1, N2, and RnaseP.
//   Each reaction: 5 uL TaqPath One-Step RT-PCR Master Mix +
//   2 uL probe/primer set + 0.1 uL Precision Blue RT Dye +
//   6.4 uL RNA extract + 6.5 uL PCR-grade water.
//   SARS-CoV-2 RNA Standard (Exact Diagnostics #COV019) run
//   as serial dilution positive control alongside each plate.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts reaction assembly on CFX384 plate.
//   Three `dispense` calls for RNA extract model the aliquoting
//   of the same extracted RNA into three separate reactions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// --- RNA aliquots for three RT-PCR channels ---
rnaAliquot_rtN1     = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen
rnaAliquot_rtN2     = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen
rnaAliquot_rtRnaseP = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen

// --- TaqPath Master Mix aliquots ---
masterMix_N1     = dispense 1 units of TaqPath_MasterMix
masterMix_N2     = dispense 1 units of TaqPath_MasterMix
masterMix_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of TaqPath_MasterMix

// --- Probe/primer set aliquots ---
primerSet_N1     = dispense 1 units of N1_ProbePrimerSet
primerSet_N2     = dispense 1 units of N2_ProbePrimerSet
primerSet_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of RnaseP_ProbePrimerSet

// --- Precision Blue RT dye aliquots ---
rtDye_N1         = dispense 1 units of PrecisionBlue_RTDye
rtDye_N2         = dispense 1 units of PrecisionBlue_RTDye
rtDye_RnaseP     = dispense 1 units of PrecisionBlue_RTDye

// --- Assemble RT-PCR reactions ---
// N1 channel
rtPCR_rxn_N1_step1 = mix masterMix_N1 with primerSet_N1 for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_N1_step2 = mix rtPCR_rxn_N1_step1 with rtDye_N1 for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_N1       = mix rtPCR_rxn_N1_step2 with rnaAliquot_rtN1 for 10s

// N2 channel
rtPCR_rxn_N2_step1 = mix masterMix_N2 with primerSet_N2 for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_N2_step2 = mix rtPCR_rxn_N2_step1 with rtDye_N2 for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_N2       = mix rtPCR_rxn_N2_step2 with rnaAliquot_rtN2 for 10s

// RnaseP channel (internal extraction control)
rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step1 = mix masterMix_RnaseP with primerSet_RnaseP for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step2 = mix rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step1 with rtDye_RnaseP for 5s
rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP       = mix rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step2 with rnaAliquot_rtRnaseP for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: RT-PCR thermocycling (CFX384 Touch, Bio-Rad).
//   CDC 2019-nCoV RT-PCR diagnostic panel (Revision 3, 2020):
//   Stage 1: Reverse transcription: 25 C / 2 min
//   Stage 2: RT incubation:         50 C / 15 min
//   Stage 3: Polymerase activation: 95 C / 2 min
//   Stage 4: 45 cycles of:
//             Denaturation:         95 C / 3 s
//             Annealing/Extension:  55 C / 30 s
//   Total estimated run time: ~80 min
//
//   NOTE: BioScript `heat` encodes each isothermal stage;
//   the 45-cycle PCR amplification is approximated as a
//   single heat step at 55 C for 45 min (45 cycles x ~60 s
//   effective per cycle at 55 C annealing/extension).
//   This is the same thermocycler abstraction used in the
//   reference BioScript files (moazami: heat at 42 C/60 s
//   and 4 C/180 s model the two-stage heat shock; the
//   multi-cycle PCR step is compressed into a single block).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// N1 thermocycle
heat rtPCR_rxn_N1 at 25c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N1 at 50c for 15m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N1 at 95c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N1 at 55c for 45m

// N2 thermocycle
heat rtPCR_rxn_N2 at 25c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N2 at 50c for 15m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N2 at 95c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_N2 at 55c for 45m

// RnaseP thermocycle (internal control)
heat rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP at 25c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP at 50c for 15m
heat rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP at 95c for 2m
heat rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP at 55c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: RT-PCR fluorescence readout (CFX Maestro software).
//   Real-time Ct values acquired during the 55 C annealing
//   steps of each cycle using FAM channel (N1, N2) and
//   Cy5/ROX channel (RnaseP, internal control).
//   Positive calling: Ct < 40 for N1 OR N2 (CDC recommendation).
//   Ct = 45 assigned to undetermined reactions (no amplification).
//   Efficiency: >99.25% for N1 and N2 (Supplementary Fig. 1).
//   Ct corresponding to 1 copy: ~38.2 (N1), ~38.6 (N2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rtPCR_N1_Signal     = detect rtPCR_N1_Detection on rtPCR_rxn_N1 for 30s
rtPCR_N2_Signal     = detect rtPCR_N2_Detection on rtPCR_rxn_N2 for 30s
rtPCR_RnaseP_Signal = detect rtPCR_RnaseP_Detection on rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: RT-PCR QC gate
// Positive call (BB2): rtPCR_N1_Signal > 0 (Ct < 40 for N1)
//   OR rtPCR_N2_Signal > 0 (Ct < 40 for N2).
//   Per CDC recommendation, a sample is called positive if
//   either N1 or N2 falls below the Ct threshold of 40.
//   BioScript does not support compound OR conditionals in a
//   single if statement; N1 signal is used as the primary
//   gate (the stronger signal per paper Fig. 2a); N2 serves
//   as a corroborating channel detected in step 15 below.
//   Paper results: 16/16 CML-positive curbside samples
//   detected by saliva RT-PCR (100% concordance; Fig. 2c,d).
// Fail (BB3): rtPCR_N1_Signal <= 0: no N1 amplification
//   detected above threshold; drain reactions.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (rtPCR_Join).
// ============================================================

if (rtPCR_N1_Signal > 0) {
    dispose rtPCR_rxn_N1
    dispose rtPCR_rxn_N2
    dispose rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP
} else {
    drain rtPCR_rxn_N1
    drain rtPCR_rxn_N2
    drain rtPCR_rxn_RnaseP
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: rtPCR_Join
// Dispose all RT-PCR signal droplets. Control falls into the
// ddPCR assay branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose rtPCR_N1_Signal
dispose rtPCR_N2_Signal
dispose rtPCR_RnaseP_Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 15: Prepare ddPCR reactions (20 uL total, 3 channels).
//   Parallel reactions targeting N1, N2, and RnaseP from the
//   same RNA extract as RT-PCR (both assays use identical
//   IDT probe/primer sets, #10006770, per paper Methods).
//   Each reaction: 5 uL One-step ddPCR Supermix + 2 uL RT
//   + 1 uL 300 mM DTT + 2 uL probe/primer set + 6.4 uL RNA.
//   NOTE: Three separate RNA aliquots dispensed from the
//   same extracted sample to model parallel reaction setup.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// --- RNA aliquots for three ddPCR channels ---
rnaAliquot_ddN1     = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen
rnaAliquot_ddN2     = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen
rnaAliquot_ddRnaseP = dispense 1 units of SalivaSpecimen

// --- ddPCR Supermix + RT aliquots ---
ddSupermix_N1     = dispense 1 units of ddPCR_Supermix_OneStep
ddSupermix_N2     = dispense 1 units of ddPCR_Supermix_OneStep
ddSupermix_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of ddPCR_Supermix_OneStep

ddRT_DTT_N1     = dispense 1 units of ReverseTranscriptase_DTT
ddRT_DTT_N2     = dispense 1 units of ReverseTranscriptase_DTT
ddRT_DTT_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of ReverseTranscriptase_DTT

// --- Probe/primer set aliquots (shared with RT-PCR IDT kit) ---
ddPrimerSet_N1     = dispense 1 units of N1_ProbePrimerSet
ddPrimerSet_N2     = dispense 1 units of N2_ProbePrimerSet
ddPrimerSet_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of RnaseP_ProbePrimerSet

// --- Assemble ddPCR reactions ---
// N1 channel
ddPCR_rxn_N1_step1 = mix ddSupermix_N1 with ddRT_DTT_N1 for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_N1_step2 = mix ddPCR_rxn_N1_step1 with ddPrimerSet_N1 for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_N1       = mix ddPCR_rxn_N1_step2 with rnaAliquot_ddN1 for 10s

// N2 channel
ddPCR_rxn_N2_step1 = mix ddSupermix_N2 with ddRT_DTT_N2 for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_N2_step2 = mix ddPCR_rxn_N2_step1 with ddPrimerSet_N2 for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_N2       = mix ddPCR_rxn_N2_step2 with rnaAliquot_ddN2 for 10s

// RnaseP channel (internal extraction control)
ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step1 = mix ddSupermix_RnaseP with ddRT_DTT_RnaseP for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step2 = mix ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step1 with ddPrimerSet_RnaseP for 5s
ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP       = mix ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP_step2 with rnaAliquot_ddRnaseP for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 16: Droplet generation (~20,000 nanoliter-sized droplets).
//   Each assembled ddPCR reaction is fractionated into
//   ~20,000 nanoliter-sized water-in-oil droplets using
//   the Bio-Rad droplet generator (manual or automated QX200).
//   Each droplet contains zero or one target RNA molecule.
//   Emulsion transferred to a 96-well plate and sealed.
//   Droplet generator oil: Bio-Rad ddPCR droplet generation oil
//   for probes (#1863005).
//   NOTE: `mix` with DropletGeneratorOil abstracts emulsification
//   step at the droplet generator; this is the key step that
//   converts a bulk PCR reaction into ~20,000 discrete
//   partitions for digital absolute quantification.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ddOil_N1     = dispense 1 units of DropletGeneratorOil
ddOil_N2     = dispense 1 units of DropletGeneratorOil
ddOil_RnaseP = dispense 1 units of DropletGeneratorOil

// NOTE: abstracts water-in-oil droplet generation
ddEmulsion_N1     = mix ddPCR_rxn_N1 with ddOil_N1 for 2m
ddEmulsion_N2     = mix ddPCR_rxn_N2 with ddOil_N2 for 2m
ddEmulsion_RnaseP = mix ddPCR_rxn_RnaseP with ddOil_RnaseP for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 17: ddPCR thermocycling (C-1000 thermal cycler, Bio-Rad).
//   Stage 1: RT:                    50 C / 60 min
//   Stage 2: Polymerase activation: 95 C / 10 min
//   Stage 3: 45 cycles of:
//             Denaturation:         95 C / 30 s
//             Annealing/Extension:  55 C / 60 s
//             (ramping speed: 2.5 C/s)
//   Stage 4: Signal stabilisation:  98 C / 10 min
//   Stage 5: Infinite hold:          4 C
//   NOTE: As for RT-PCR, the 45-cycle amplification is
//   compressed into a single heat step at 55 C for 45 min.
//   The 98 C signal stabilisation step is encoded separately.
//   The 4 C infinite hold is encoded as 4 C for 60 m
//   (1 h approximation; protocol allows overnight hold).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// N1 emulsion thermocycle
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 25c for 2m
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 50c for 60m
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 95c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 55c for 45m
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 98c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_N1 at 4c for 60m

// N2 emulsion thermocycle
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 25c for 2m
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 50c for 60m
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 95c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 55c for 45m
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 98c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_N2 at 4c for 60m

// RnaseP emulsion thermocycle (internal control)
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 25c for 2m
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 50c for 60m
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 95c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 55c for 45m
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 98c for 10m
heat ddEmulsion_RnaseP at 4c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 18: Droplet reading - QX200 droplet reader (Bio-Rad).
//   Raw fluorescence amplitude data extracted to Quantasoft
//   software (Bio-Rad) for downstream analysis.
//   FAM channel: N1 and N2 TaqMan probes (SARS-CoV-2 targets).
//   HEX/VIC channel: RnaseP probe (internal control).
//   Output: CN/uL (copy number per microlitre) and positive
//   droplet count for each channel.
//
//   POSITIVE CALLING (saliva specimens, empirical threshold):
//   A specimen is called positive when EITHER N1 OR N2 shows
//   BOTH CN/uL AND positive droplet count above the empirical
//   threshold (mean + 2*SD from 45 pre-operative negatives;
//   Supplementary Table 2).
//   LOD: N1 = 0.06 CN/uL; N2 = 0.21 CN/uL (Supplementary Fig. 2).
//   LOD (dilution series): detects N1 at 1:1,000,000 dilution
//   in pool of negative specimens (Supplementary Table 1).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ddPCR_N1_Signal     = detect ddPCR_N1_Detection on ddEmulsion_N1 for 30s
ddPCR_N2_Signal     = detect ddPCR_N2_Detection on ddEmulsion_N2 for 30s
ddPCR_RnaseP_Signal = detect ddPCR_RnaseP_Detection on ddEmulsion_RnaseP for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: ddPCR QC gate
// Positive call (BB5): ddPCR_N1_Signal > 0 (CN/uL and droplet
//   count exceed empirical threshold for N1).
//   N1 used as primary gate (stronger LOD: 0.06 vs 0.21 CN/uL).
//   Paper results: 15/16 CML-positive curbside samples
//   detected (93.75% concordance); 31/92 total positives
//   identified by ddPCR vs 16/92 by CML NS assay (Fig. 2e,f).
//   Independent re-test of 46 saliva specimens confirmed
//   91.3% reproducibility (Supplementary Fig. 8).
// Fail (BB6): ddPCR_N1_Signal <= 0: signal below empirical
//   threshold; drain emulsion droplets.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ddPCR_N1_Signal > 0) {
    dispose ddEmulsion_N1
    dispose ddEmulsion_N2
    dispose ddEmulsion_RnaseP
} else {
    drain ddEmulsion_N1
    drain ddEmulsion_N2
    drain ddEmulsion_RnaseP
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all ddPCR signal droplets and RNA QC signal.
// Dispose RNA extract. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose ddPCR_N1_Signal
dispose ddPCR_N2_Signal
dispose ddPCR_RnaseP_Signal
dispose rnaQcSignal
dispose rnaExtract

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
